/*
init
----

Adds the `--init` flag when the dev container is created, so **tini** runs as
PID 1.

Why use it?
• Tini is a tiny init system that reaps orphaned child processes, preventing
  “zombie” PIDs.
• It also forwards Unix signals, letting your app shut down cleanly.

Default: **false**.
The option works across orchestrators that support the `--init` flag.

More details: https://github.com/krallin/tini
*/

{
  "name": "1_11-spec_init",
  "image": "ubuntu:latest",
  "init": true
}
